irmation)", "Vitamin D toxicity: no history of supplementation to support this mechanism"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Altered mental status (trouble focusing)", "Hypercalcemia with elevated alkaline phosphatase"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Primary Hyperparathyroidism with Hypercalcemia", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.052, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The patient's young age (45yo) and African American ethnicity moderately argue against primary hyperparathyroidism as the cause."]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Malignancy with Hypercalcemia", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.16294764463312414, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Normal physical exam and young age moderately contradict the expected presentation of malignancy-related hypercalcemia."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["humoral hypercalcemia of malignancy", "multiple myeloma", "squamous cell carcinoma", "primary hyperparathyroidism"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Vitamin-D / Granulomatous Hypercalcemia", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.13392857142857142, "posterior": 0.6886842119718702, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Elevated alkaline phosphatase shows weak support for PHPT and other hypercalcemia categories, but insufficient evidence to distinguish between PHPT and maligna…"], "evidence_against": ["Absence of vitamin D supplementation history moderately argues against vitamin D excess as the cause."], "unresolved_questions": [], "chil